      "editorial": {
        "en": {
          "why_it_matters": "Violin and cello are not ornamental here; they are the front line. ZARUKAME has built its identity around making those two strings carry melody, attack, harmony and dramatic weight normally assigned to a singer or horn section. Expanding the duo with piano, guitar and drums at its first Billboard Live appearance should expose how that string language behaves when it has a real rhythm section underneath it.",
          "trip_verdict": "Worth keeping on the Tokyo board and attending if the night is open, especially if string sound and instrumental crossover are part of the trip. It is a strong club date rather than something that should displace a rarer master, premiere or one-off encounter.",
