      "editorial": {
        "en": {
          "why_it_matters": "Ohashi Trio is useful to the RADAR precisely because the project refuses a clean border between singer-songwriter craft and instrumental arrangement. This Billboard run puts that writing into a jazz-based sextet with Marty Holoubek on bass, two keyboard/guitar voices and saxophone around Ohashi's own multi-instrumental center. In a small room, the value is hearing how pop songs are reharmonized and made to groove as an ensemble rather than simply reproduced from the record.",
          "trip_verdict": "Actively make room for one of the Tokyo sets if contemporary Japanese arranging, groove and multi-instrumental songwriting are part of the trip. The same sextet format also plays Yokohama and Osaka, so this is a strong night to prioritize rather than a scarce date that should dictate the entire itinerary.",
